    "review": "One fixed11-label program resets an arbitrary initial accumulator by actual subtraction, reads two actual arrays, sums their squared differences, and never writes memory. Every legal standalone trace returns the actual sum in real register0 at9N+3 with that charged-cost bound. Every valid literal caller embedding at arbitrary trace time returns running at mapped local halt10 at9N+2, with actual sum, unchanged memory and caller-prefix cost plus9N+2. N=0 and arbitrary overlapping arrays are included.",
